      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk thats a pretty big claim to say they just borrowed everything. i read that they actually made huge leaps in algebra and medicine that the Greeks hadn't even touched. if we're talking about \"foundations of the modern world,\" shouldn't we look at how these different cultures interacted instead of just saying one was the pioneer and the others were just copies? it feels like you're kind of dismissing a lot of non-European history as less important.",
